@attribute [Route($"{GlobalValues.Root_path_Components}/{GlobalValues.Component_Path_Part_GoTo}/{GlobalValues.Common_Page_Path_Installation}")]

<PageTitle>@GlobalValues.Component_Name_GoTo @GlobalValues.Common_Page_Title_Installation</PageTitle>

<h1>@GlobalValues.Component_Name_GoTo @GlobalValues.Common_Page_Title_Installation</h1>

<GoTo LabelText="GoTo installation page heading" />
<p>
    <strong>Note: </strong> It is a requirement that the Blazor Ramp Core <span class="@CodeSpan.Base">core-live-region.js</span> script, <span class="@CodeSpan.Base">LiveRegionService</span>, and
    associated <span class="@CodeSpan.Base">&lt;AnnouncementHistory /&gt;</span> component are added alongside this component’s specific
    requirements (a stylesheet reference in this instance).
</p>
<p>
    You do not need to add the BlazorRamp.Core package separately, as BlazorRamp.Core is included as a transitive package, you only need to add the packages that contain the components
    that you wish to use i.e the <b>BlazorRamp.GoTo</b> NuGet package.
</p>
<p>
    Please follow the instructions in the <a class="@GlobalValues.Link_Class" href="@($"{GlobalValues.Root_Path}{GlobalValues.Common_Page_Path_Installation}")">@GlobalValues.Getting_Started_Name - @GlobalValues.Common_Page_Title_Installation</a>
    ensuring that in the <span class="@CodeSpan.Base">&lt;head&gt;</span> section you also add the GoTo stylesheet as follows:
</p>
<CodeBox CodeBlock="@GoToSnippets.Add_GoTo_Style_Sheet" AriaLabel="Add GoTo stylesheet code block" />
<p>
    The GoTo viewer and its triggering button are designed to be globally available using a single instance.
    The simplest approach is to place this above the <span class="@CodeSpan.Base">Router</span> component which dependant on your project will either be inside the 
    <span class="@CodeSpan.Base">App.razor</span> or <span class="@CodeSpan.Base">Routes.razor</span> file.
</p>
<p>
    If you accept all the defaults then you can simply just place <span class="@CodeSpan.Base">&lt;GoToViewer /&gt;</span> in the file with the <span class="@CodeSpan.Base">Router</span> component.
</p>
<p>
    Bwlow is the component with all the default values being used to set the parameters. This code along with the other components shown, is what is being used on this site.
</p>
<p>
    <strong>Important</strong> This site is a global WebAssembly site so everything is interactive so no <span class="@CodeSpan.Base">rendermode</span> needs to be explicitly set. If you are using InteractiveAuto for both
    Server and WebAssembly then add the rendermode to the component for example: <span class="@CodeSpan.Base">&ltGoToViewer @@rendermode="InteractiveAuto" /&gt;</span>.
</p>


<CodeBox CodeBlock="@GoToSnippets.Placement_On_Router_Page" AriaLabel="Component placement for global usage example" />

